hadiths[112]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1541","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) sat on the pulpit and said, ""Allah has given one of His Slaves the choice of receiving the splendor and luxury of the worldly life whatever he likes or to accept the good (of the Hereafter) which is with Allah. So he has chosen that good which is with Allah."" On that Abu Bakr wept and said, ""Our fathers and mothers be sacrificed for you."" We became astonished at this. The people said, ""Look at this old man! Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) talks about a Slave of Allah to whom He has given the option to choose either the splendor of this worldly life or the good which is with Him, while he says. 'our fathers and mothers be sacrifice(i for you."" But it was Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) who had been given option, and Abu Bakr knew it better than we. Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) added, ""No doubt, I am indebted to Abu Bakr more than to anybody else regarding both his companionship and his wealth. And if I had to take a Khalil from my followers, I would certainly have taken Abu Bakr, but the fraternity of Islam is. sufficient. Let no door (i.e. Khoukha) of the Mosque remain open, except the door of Abu Bakr."""""""
"1542","The Prophet (ﷺ) deputed me to read the Army of Dhat-as-Salasil. I came to him and said, Who is the most beloved person to you?"" He said"""
"1543","A woman came to the Prophet (ﷺ) who ordered her to return to him again. She said, What if I came and did not find you?"" as if she wanted to say"""
"1544","Once Allah's Messenger (ﷺ); offered the morning prayer and then faced the people and said, ""While a man was driving a cow, he suddenly rode over it and beat it. The cow said, ""We have not been created for this, but we have been created for sloughing."" On that the people said astonishingly, ""Glorified be Allah! A cow speaks!"" The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""I believe this, and Abu Bakr and `Umar too, believe it, although neither of them was present there. While a person was amongst his sheep, a wolf attacked and took one of the sheep. The man chased the wolf till he saved it from the wolf, where upon the wolf said, 'You have saved it from me; but who will guard it on the day of the wild beasts when there will be no shepherd to guard them except me (because of riots and afflictions)? ' "" The people said surprisingly, ""Glorified be Allah! A wolf speaks!"" The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""But I believe this, and Abu Bakr and `Umar too, believe this, although neither of them was present there."" (See the Foot-note of page No. 10 Vol.5)"""
"1545","Narrated Ibn `Abbas:\n\nWhen (the dead body of) `Umar was put on his deathbed, the people gathered around him and invoked \n(Allah) and prayed for him before the body was taken away, and I was amongst them. Suddenly I felt \nsomebody taking hold of my shoulder and found out that he was `Ali bin Abi Talib. `Ali invoked \nAllah's Mercy for `Umar and said, \O `Umar! You have not left behind you a person whose deeds I \nlike to imitate and meet Allah with more than I like your deeds. By Allah! I always thought that Allah \nwould keep you with your two companions"""
"1546","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, While I was sleeping"""
"1547","This hadith has been narrated on the same authority by Ubaidullah. And in the narration of Abu Bakr (the words are): More than three (days)."" Ibn Numair narrated on the authority of his father"""
"1548","The hadith of Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I heard the Prophet (peace be upon him) say: ""While I was asleep, I saw myself at a well with a bucket on it. I drew from it as much as Allah willed. Then Abu Bakr (son of Abu Quhafah) took it and drew one or two buckets, and there was weakness in his drawing, and Allah will forgive his weakness. Then it became a large bucket, and Umar ibn al-Khattab took it. I have never seen anyone among the people draw water with such strength as Umar drew, until the people gathered at the watering place."""""""
"1549","Narrated `Abdullah bin `Umar:\n\nThe Prophet (ﷺ) said, \In a dream I saw myself drawing water from a well with a bucket. Abu Bakr came \nand drew a bucket or two weakly. May Allah forgive him. Then `Umar bin Al-Khattab came and the \nbucket turned into a very large one in his hands. I had never seen such a mighty person as he in doing \nsuch hard work till all the people drank to their satisfaction and watered their camels that knelt down \nthere."""""""
"1550","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, He who is not merciful to others"""
"1551","While we were in the company of the Prophet, he said, While I was asleep ""1552"",A man heard another man reciting (in the prayers): 'Say (O Muhammad): He is Allah"""
"1552","[AI-translation] Hadith of Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas, who said: Umar asked permission to enter upon the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, while there were women from Quraysh with him, talking to him a lot, raising their voices. When Umar asked permission, they rushed to the screen. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, gave him permission to enter, while the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, was laughing. Umar said: May Allah keep you smiling, O Messenger of Allah. He said: I am amazed at these women who were with me; when they heard your voice, they rushed to the screen. Umar said: You, O Messenger of Allah, were more worthy that they should be in awe of you. Then he said: O enemies of your own souls, do you fear me and not fear the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him? They said: Yes, for you are harsher and sterner than the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, the Shaitan never encounters you taking a path except that he takes a path other than your path.""
1553"""
"1553","Narrated Ibn 'Umar: When 'Abdullah (bin Ubai) died, his son 'Abdullah bin 'Abdullah came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and asked him to give him his shirt in which he might shroud his father. He gave it to him, and then he asked him to offer the funeral prayer over him. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) got up to offer the prayer, but 'Umar got up and caught hold of the garment of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: ""O Messenger of Allah, will you pray over him although your Lord has forbidden you to pray over him?"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Allah has only given me the choice, for He said: 'Ask forgiveness for them, or do not ask forgiveness for them; (even) if you ask forgiveness for them seventy times...' and I shall increase it beyond seventy."" 'Umar said: ""He is a hypocrite."" (Ibn 'Umar) said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) offered the prayer over him, and then Allah revealed: ""And never (O Muhammad) pray (funeral prayer) for any of them (hypocrites) who dies, nor stand at his grave."""
"1554","That he was in the company of the Prophet (ﷺ) in one of the gardens of Medina and in the hand of the Prophet there was a stick, and he was striking (slowly) the water and the mud with it. A man came (at the gate of the garden) and asked permission to enter. The Prophet (ﷺ) said, Open the gate for him and give him the glad tidings of entering Paradise. ""I went"""
"1555","I performed ablution in my house and then went out and said, Today I shall stick to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) and stay with him all this day of mine (in his service)."" I went to the Mosque and asked about the Prophet . They said"""
"1556","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) set out for Tabuk. appointing `Ali as his deputy (in Medina). `Ali said, ""Do you want to leave me with the children and women?"" The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""Will you not be pleased that you will be to me like Aaron to Moses? But there will be no prophet after me."""""""
"1557","On the day of Khaibar, Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, Tomorrow I will give this flag to a man through whose hands Allah will give us victory. He loves Allah and His Apostle ""1558"",Al-Bara' reported that Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) had the most handsome face amongst men and he had the best disposition and he was neither very tall nor short-statured"""
"1558","[AI-translation] Akwa', may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, stayed behind from the Prophet, peace be upon him, at Khaybar, and he had eye inflammation. He said: Shall I stay behind from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him? So Ali went out and caught up with the Prophet, peace be upon him. When it was the evening of the night whose morning it was conquered, the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: I will certainly give the banner tomorrow, or he said: A man will certainly take it tomorrow, whom Allah and His Messenger love, or he said: who loves Allah and His Messenger, whom Allah will grant victory. Behold, there was Ali, and what we hoped for. They said: This is Ali. So the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, gave it to him, and Allah granted him victory.""
1559"""
"1559","Narrated Sahl bin Sa'd: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to the house of Fatimah but did not find 'Ali in the house. He said, ""Where is your cousin?"" She said, ""There was something between us and he got angry with me and left, and he did not sleep here."" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to a man, ""Look where he is."" He came and said, ""O Messenger of Allah, he is in the mosque, sleeping."" So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to him while he was lying down, and his cloak had fallen off his side, and dust had gotten on him. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) began wiping the dust off him, saying, ""Get up, O Abu Turab! Get up, O Abu Turab!"""
"1560","Abu Burda b. Abu Musa al-Ash'ari reported:'Abdullah b. Umar said to me: Did you hear anything from your father narrating something from the messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about the time on Friday? I said: Yes, I heard him say from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) (these words): It is between the time when the Imam sits down and the end of the prayer"""""""
"1561","Narrated `Ali:\n\nI never saw the Prophet (ﷺ) saying, \Let my parents sacrifice their lives for you"""
"1562","Narrated Sa`d:\n\nOn the day of the battle of Uhud the Prophet (ﷺ) mentioned for me both his parents (i.e. saying, \Let my \nparents be sacrificed for you.\"")."""" ""1563"",*.rr.r- but Talha and Sa'd"""
"1563","[AI-translation] Hadith of Talhah and Sa'd from Abu 'Uthman, who said: None remained with the Prophet, peace be upon him, on one of those days in which the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, fought, except Talhah and Sa'd, from their narration.""
1564"""
"1564","Narrated Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""Who will bring me news of the (enemy) people on the day of Al-Ahzab (the Confederates)?"" Az-Zubair said, ""I (will)."" Then he again said, ""Who will bring me news of the people?"" Az-Zubair said, ""I (will)."" The Prophet (ﷺ) then said, ""Every Prophet has a disciple (Hawari), and my disciple is Az-Zubair."""
"1565","During the battle of Al-Ahzab, I and `Umar bin Abi-Salama were kept behind with the women. Behold! I saw (my father) Az-Zubair riding his horse, going to and coming from Bani Quraiza twice or thrice. So when I came back I said, O my father! I saw you going to and coming from Bani Quraiza?"" He said"""
"1566","Once `Umar bin `Abdul `Aziz sat on his throne in the courtyard of his house so that the people might gather before him. Then he admitted them and (when they came in), he said, What do you think of Al-Qasama?"" They said"""
"1567","The Prophet (ﷺ) said to the people of Nijran, I will send you the most trustworthy man."" (Every one of) the companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) was looking forward (to be that person). He then sent Abu 'Ubaida."""""""
"1568","Once the Prophet (ﷺ) went out during the day. Neither did he talk to me nor I to him till he reached the market of Bani Qainuqa and then he sat in the compound of Fatima's house and asked about the small boy (his grandson Al-Hasan) but Fatima kept the boy in for a while. I thought she was either changing his clothes or giving the boy a bath. After a while the boy came out running and the Prophet (ﷺ) embraced and kissed him and then said, 'O Allah! Love him, and love whoever loves him.' ""1569"",Yazid reported:Salama sought to say prayer near the pillar which was by that place where copies of the Qur'an were kept. I said to him: Abu Muslim. I see you striving to offer your prayer by this pillar. He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) seeking to pray by its side"""
"1569","[AI-translation] Bara', may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I saw the Prophet, peace be upon him, with Al-Hasan on his shoulder, saying: O Allah, I love him, so love him.""
1570"""
"1570","Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Umar: Zaid bin Harithah, the freed slave of Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), we used not to call him but Zaid bin Muhammad, until there was revealed in the Qur'an: ""Call them by (the names of) their fathers, that is more just in the sight of Allah."""
"1571","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) sent an army unit headed by Usama bin Zaid and the people criticized his leadership. The Prophet (ﷺ) said (to the people), If you are criticizing his leadership now ""1572"",Narrated Ibn Abi Mulaika:\n\nIbn Az-Zubair said to Ibn Ja`far \Do you remember when I"""
"1572","[AI-translation] Hadith of Abdullah bin Jafar: Ibn Al-Zubayr said to Ibn Jafar, may Allah be pleased with them both: Do you remember when we met the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, I, you, and Ibn Abbas? He said: Yes, he carried us and left you.""
1573"""
"1573","Narrated 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him): I heard the Prophet (ﷺ) say, ""The best of its women is Mary, the daughter of 'Imran, and the best of its women is Khadijah."""
"1574","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, Many amongst men attained perfection but amongst women none attained the perfection except Mary"""
"1575","Hilal b. Yasaf reported that a person got angry and slapped his slave-girl. Thereupon Suwaid b. Muqarrin said to him:You could find no other part (to slap) but the prominent part of her face. See I was one of the seven sons of Muqarrin, and we had but only one slave-girl. The youngest of us slapped her, and Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) commanded us to set her free"""
"1576","Narrated Isma`il:\n\nI asked `Abdullah bin Abi `Aufa, \Did the Prophet (ﷺ) give glad tidings to Khadija?\"" He said"""
"1577","Narrated `Aisha:\n\nI did not feel jealous of any of the wives of the Prophet (ﷺ) as much as I did of Khadija though I did not \nsee her, but the Prophet (ﷺ) used to mention her very often, and when ever he slaughtered a sheep, he \nwould cut its parts and send them to the women friends of Khadija. When I sometimes said to him, \n\(You treat Khadija in such a way) as if there is no woman on earth except Khadija"""
"1578","Narrated 'Aisha: Once Hala bint Khuwailid, Khadija's sister, asked the permission of the Prophet (ﷺ) to enter. On that, the Prophet (ﷺ) remembered the way Khadija used to ask permission, and that upset him. He said, \O Allah! Hala!\"" So I became jealous and said"""
"1579","Aisha reported that the Prophet, peace be upon him, said to her: “I have seen you in a dream twice. I saw you in a silk garment, and someone said, ‘This is your wife; uncover her.’ When it was uncovered, it was you. I said, ‘If this is from Allah, then it is decreed.’”"""
"1580","That Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said to her, I know when you are pleased with me or angry with me."" I said"""
"1581","Narrated `Aisha:I used to play with the dolls in the presence of the Prophet, and my girl friends also used to play with me. When Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) used to enter (my dwelling place) they used to hide themselves, but the Prophet would call them to join and play with me. (The playing with the dolls and similar images is forbidden, but it was allowed for `Aisha at that time, as she was a little girl, not yet reached the age of puberty.) (Fath-ul-Bari page 143, Vol)"""
"1582","Abu Huraira reported Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) as saying:I am most akin to Jesus Christ among the whole of mankind, and all the Prophets are of different mothers but belong to one religion and no Prophet was raised between me and Jesus"""
"1583","Abdullah reported that Allah's Messenger (may peace be upol him) got fashioned a signet ring of gold but he kept its stone on the inner side of his palm as he wore it, so the people (following his example) got fashioned (such rings). Then one day as he sat on the pulpit he pulled it away saying:I wore this ring and kept its stone towards the inner side. He then threw it away, and said: By Allah, I will never wear it; so the people threw their rings away"""
"1584","Narrated `Aisha:\n\nI heard the Prophet (ﷺ) and listened to him before his death while he was leaning his back on me and \nsaying, \O Allah! Forgive me"""
"1585","Abu Bakra wrote to his son who was in Sijistan: 'Do not judge between two persons when you are angry, for I heard the Prophet (ﷺ) saying, A judge should not judge between two persons while he is in an angry mood."""""""""
"1586","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) used to practice I`tikaf every year in the month of Ramadan. And after offering the morning prayer, he used to enter the place of his I`tikaf. `Aisha asked his permission to let her practice I`tikaf and he allowed her, and so she pitched a tent in the mosque. When Hafsa heard of that, she also pitched a tent (for herself), and when Zainab heard of that, she too pitched another tent. When, in the morning, Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) had finished the morning prayer, he saw four tents and asked, What is this?"" He was informed about it. He then said ""1587"",Anas reported a hadith like this from Allah's Apostle (ﷺ) through another chain of transmitters"""
"1587","[AI-translation] Hadith of Aishah, that the Prophet, peace be upon him, when he went out, would draw lots among his wives. The lot fell to Aishah and Hafsah. And the Prophet, peace be upon him, when it was night, would travel with Aishah, conversing. Hafsah said: Will you not ride my camel tonight and I will ride yours, so you can look and I can look? She said: Yes. So she rode. The Prophet, peace be upon him, came to Aishah's camel, and Hafsah was on it. He greeted her with salam, then traveled until they dismounted. Aishah missed him. When they dismounted, she put her legs among the idhkhir and said: O Lord, send upon me a scorpion or a snake to bite me, for I cannot say anything to him.""
1588"""
"1588","Narrated Anas bin Malik: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: ""The superiority of 'Aishah to other women is like the superiority of Tharid to other kinds of food."""
"1589","[AI-translation] Hadith of Aishah, that the Prophet, peace be upon him, said to her: O Aishah, this is Jibril, he conveys salam upon you. She said: And upon him be salam, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. You see what I do not see, meaning the Prophet, peace be upon him.""
1590"""
"1590","Narrated 'Aishah: Eleven women sat together and promised and pledged to conceal nothing of the affairs of their husbands.

The first said: My husband is like the meat of a lean camel placed on the top of a mountain which is neither easy to climb, nor is the meat fat so that one might put up with the trouble of fetching it.

The second said: I will not disclose my husband's secrets, for I fear I shall not be able to leave anything out; for if I mention him, I will mention his faults and blemishes, all of them.

The third said: My husband is tall; if I describe him, I shall be divorced; and if I keep silent, I shall be left in suspense.

The fourth said: My husband is like the night of Tihamah, neither hot nor cold; neither fearsome nor tiresome.

The fifth said: My husband, when he enters the house, is like a leopard; and when he goes out, he is like a lion. He does not ask about what he has left in the house.

The sixth said: My husband, if he eats, eats too much, leaving nothing; and if he drinks, he drinks up all; and if he lies down, he wraps himself up and does not put his hand inside (towards me) to know my grief.

The seventh said: My husband is impotent, or foolish and confused. Every kind of ailment afflicts him. He may break your head, or wound your body, or do both to you.

The eighth said: My husband is soft to touch like a rabbit, and he smells sweet like the perfume called Zarnab.

The ninth said: My husband is a tall man with respect to the columns of his house, and long as to his baldric; his house is spacious, and his fire is often kindled for cooking or for guests, and his house is near the meeting place (of the people) so that whenever they meet, they will call on him.

The tenth said: My husband is Malik, and Malik is a wonderful man, far better than that. He has many camels with plenty of resting places (in his yard) but few pastures (i.e. he has many camels which stay near his house so that they may be slaughtered generously for guests, unlike those whose camels are away grazing), and whenever the camels hear the sound of the tambourine (or lute), they realize that they will be slaughtered (for guests).

The eleventh said: My husband is Abu Zar', and what do you know about Abu Zar'? He has given me many ornaments, and my ears are heavy with them, and my arms have become fat (i.e. I have become fat). He has pleased me, and I have become so glad. He found me with my family who were mere owners of sheep and living in poverty, and he brought me to a respected family who possessed horses and camels, and where wheat and grains were sifted (i.e. a life of luxury). Whatever I say, he does not rebuke or reproach me. When I sleep, I sleep till late in the morning, and when I drink water (or milk), I drink my fill. The mother of Abu Zar'! And what do you know about the mother of Abu Zar'? Her saddlebags were always full (of provisions for guests), and her house was spacious. As for the son of Abu Zar', what do you know about the son of Abu Zar'? He uses his mother's outstretched leather bed as his own bed, being as slim as an arrow drawn out of its quiver, and he is satisfied by eating the meat of a small kid. As for the daughter of Abu Zar', what do you know about the daughter of Abu Zar'? She is obedient to her father and to her mother. She has a fat well-built body which fills her garment and pleases her husband. As for the slave-girl of Abu Zar', what do you know about the slave-girl of Abu Zar'? She does not disclose our secrets, but keeps them, and does not waste our provisions, and does not leave the sweepings scattered around our house.

She (the woman) added: One day Abu Zar' went out at the time when the milk was being milked (from the animals), and he saw a woman who had two sons like leopards playing with her two breasts. (On seeing her) my husband divorced me and married her. Thereafter I married a noble man who used to ride a fast tireless horse, and he took a spear in his hand, and gave me many things, and also gave me a pair of every kind of livestock, and said, ""Eat (of this), O Umm Zar', and provide for your relatives."" She added: Even if I gathered together all the things he gave me, they would not fill the smallest utensil of Abu Zar'.

'Aishah added: Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said to me: ""I am to you as Abu Zar' was to Umm Zar'."""
"1591","Narrated `Ali bin Al-Husain:\n\nThat when they reached Medina after returning from Yazid bin Mu'awaiya after the martyrdom of \nHusain bin `Ali (may Allah bestow His Mercy upon him), Al-Miswar bin Makhrama met him and said \nto him, \Do you have any need you may order me to satisfy?\"" `Ali said"""
"1592","Who, from among Ka`b's sons, was the guide of Ka`b when he became blind: I heard Ka`b bin Malik narrating the story of (the Ghazwa of) Tabuk in which he failed to take part. Ka`b said, I did not remain behind Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) in any Ghazwa that he fought except the Ghazwa of Tabuk"""
"1593","Mother of the Believers: We, the wives of the Prophet (ﷺ) were all sitting with the Prophet (ﷺ) and none of us had left when Fatima came walking, and by Allah, her gait was very similar to that of Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) .' When he saw her, he welcomed her, saying, Welcome"""
"1594","I got the news that Gabriel came to the Prophet (ﷺ) while Um Salama was present. Gabriel started talking (to the Prophet (ﷺ) and then left. The Prophet (ﷺ) said to Um Salama, ""(Do you know) who it was?"" (or a similar question). She said, ""It was Dihya (a handsome person amongst the companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) )."" Later on Um Salama said, ""By Allah! I thought he was none but Dihya, till I heard the Prophet (ﷺ) talking about Gabriel in his sermon."" (The Sub-narrator asked Abu `Uthman, ""From where have you heard this narration?"" He replied, ""From Usama bin Zaid."")"""
"1595","Narrated `Aisha:\n\nSome of the wives of the Prophet (ﷺ) asked him, \Who amongst us will be the first to follow you (i.e. die \nafter you)?\"" He said"""
"1596","The Prophet (ﷺ) used not to enter any house in Medina except the house of Um Sulaim besides those of his wives when he was asked why, he said, I take pity on her as her brother was killed in my company. """""""""
"1597","Narrated Abu Musa Al-Ash`ari:\n\nMy brother and I came from Yemen, and for some time we continued to consider `Abdullah bin \nMas`ud as one of the members of the family of the Prophet (ﷺ) because we used to see him and his mother \ngoing in the house of the Prophet (ﷺ) very often."""
"1598","Once 'Abdullah bin Mas'0d delivered a Khutba (religious talk) before us and said, By Allah"""
"1599","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, ""There are three persons whom Allah will not look at on the Day of Resurrection, nor will he purify them and theirs shall be a severe punishment. They are: -1. A man possessed superfluous water, on a way and he withheld it from travelers. -2. A man who gave a pledge of allegiance to a ruler and he gave it only for worldly benefits. If the ruler gives him something he gets satisfied, and if the ruler withholds something from him, he gets dissatisfied. -3. And man displayed his goods for sale after the `Asr prayer and he said, 'By Allah, except Whom None has the right to be worshipped, I have been given so much for my goods,' and somebody believes him (and buys them). The Prophet (ﷺ) then recited: ""Verily! Those who purchase a little gain at the cost of Allah's Covenant and their oaths."" (3.77)"""
"1600","`Abdullah (bin Mas`ud) was mentioned before `Abdullah bin `Amr. The latter said, That is a man I continue to love because I heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) saying"""
"1601","On the day of Badr, the Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""Who will go and see what has happened to Abu Jahl?"" Ibn Mas`ud went and found that the two sons of 'Afra had struck him fatally. `Abdullah bin Mas`ud got hold of his beard and said, ""'Are you Abu Jahl?"" He replied, ""Can there be a man more superior to one whom his own folk have killed (or you have killed)?"""" ""1602"",The Prophet (ﷺ) said to Ubai (bin Ka`b). Allah has ordered me to recite to you:--'Those who disbelieve among the people of the Scripture and among the idolators are not going to stop (from their disbelief.') (Sura 98) Ubai said"""
"1602","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, peace be upon him, said to Ubayy: ""Indeed Allah has commanded me to recite to you: 'Lam yakuni alladhina kafaru'."" He said: ""Did He name me?"" He said: ""Yes."" So he wept.""
1603"""
"1603","Narrated Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him): I heard the Prophet (ﷺ) say: ""The Throne shook for the death of Sa'd bin Mu'adh."""
"1604","A silken cloth was given as a present to the Prophet (ﷺ) . His companions started touching it and admiring its softness. The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""Are you admiring its softness? The handkerchiefs of Sa`d bin Mu`adh (in Paradise) are better and softer than it."""""""
"1605","A silken cloak was presented to the Prophet (ﷺ) and he used to forbid the usage of silk (by men). When the people were fascinated by the cloak. he said, By Allah in Whose Hands the life of Muhammad is"""
"1606","On the day of the Battle of Uhud, my father was brought and he had been mutilated (in battle) and was placed in front of Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) and a sheet was over him. I went intending to uncover my father but my people forbade me; again I wanted to uncover him but my people forbade me. Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) gave his order and he was shifted away. At that time he heard the voice of a crying woman and asked, Who is this?"" They said"""
"1607","While I was walking with the Prophet (ﷺ) at the Hurra of Medina in the evening, the mountain of Uhud appeared before us. The Prophet (ﷺ) said, O Abu Dhar! I would not like to have gold equal to Uhud (mountain) for me"""
"1608","The hadith of Jarir (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) never screened me off since I embraced Islam, nor did he ever see me except that he smiled in my face. And I complained to him that I could not sit firmly on horses, so he struck my chest with his hand and said: ""O Allah, make him firm and make him a guide and rightly guided."""""""
"1609","The Hadith of Jarir: He said, the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said to me: ""Will you not relieve me of Dhu al-Khalasah?"" It was a house belonging to Khath'am called the Yemeni Ka'bah. He said: So I departed with one hundred and fifty horsemen from Ahmas, who were horsemen. He said: I could not sit firmly on horseback, so he struck my chest until I saw the marks of his fingers on my chest, and said: ""O Allah, make him steadfast and make him a guide and rightly guided."" So I went to it, demolished it and burned it. Then he sent word to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) informing him. Jarir's messenger said: ""By Him Who sent you with the truth, I did not come to you until I had left it like a hollow camel, or a mangy one."" He said: So he blessed the horses of Ahmas and their men five times."""
"1610","Narrated Ibn `Abbas:\n\nThe Prophet (ﷺ) used to say, \I seek refuge (with YOU) by Your 'Izzat"""
"1611","In the lifetime of the Prophet (ﷺ) whosoever saw a dream would narrate it to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ). I had a wish of seeing a dream to narrate it to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) (p.b.u.h) I was a grown up boy and used to sleep in the Mosque in the lifetime of the Prophet. I saw in the dream that two angels caught hold of me and took me to the Fire which was built all round like a built well and had two poles in it and the people in it were known to me. I started saying, I seek refuge with Allah from the Fire."" Then I met another angel who told me not to be afraid. I narrated the dream to Hafsa who told it to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ). The Prophet said"""
"1612","Narrated Umm Sulaim that she said, O Allih's Messenger! Anas is you servant ""1613"",Anas b. Malik reported that Allah's Apostle (ﷺ) told me something secretly. I informed none about that and Umm Sulaim asked me about it"""
"1613","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas ibn Malik: The Prophet, peace be upon him, confided a secret to me, and I have not told anyone of it after him. And Umm Sulaym asked me, but I did not tell her of it.""
1614"""
"1614","Narrated Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas: I never heard the Prophet (ﷺ) say about anyone walking upon the earth that he was one of the people of Paradise except concerning 'Abdullah bin Salam. He said: And it was concerning him that this verse was revealed: ""And a witness from among the Children of Israel bore witness..."" (46:10)"
"1615","While I was sitting in the Mosque of Medina, there entered a man (Abdullah bin Salam) with signs of solemnity over his face. The people said, ""He is one of the people of Paradise."" He prayed two light rak`at and then left. I followed him and said, ""When you entered the Mosque, the people said, 'He is one of the people of Paradise.' "" He said, ""By Allah, one ought not say what he does not know; and I will tell you why. In the lifetime of the Prophet (ﷺ) I had a dream which I narrated to him. I saw as if I were in a garden."" He then described its extension and greenery. He added: In its center there was an iron pillar whose lower end was fixed in the earth and the upper end was in the sky, and at its upper end there was a (ring-shaped) hand-hold. I was told to climb it. I said, ""I can't."" ""Then a servant came to me and lifted my clothes from behind and I climbed till I reached the top (of the pillar). Then I got hold of the hand-hold, and I was told to hold it tightly, then I woke up and (the effect of) the handhold was in my hand. I narrated al I that to the Prophet (ﷺ) who said, 'The garden is Islam, and the handhold is the Most Truth-worthy Hand-Hold. So you will remain as a Muslim till you die."" The narrator added: ""The man was `Abdullah bin Salam."""""""
"1616","`Umar came to the Mosque while Hassan was reciting a poem. (`Umar disapproved of that). On that Hassan said, I used to recite poetry in this very Mosque in the presence of one (i.e. the Prophet (ﷺ) ) who was better than you."" Then he turned towards Abu Huraira and said (to him) ""1617"",It is narrated on the authority of Thabit b. Dahhak that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) observed:He who took deliberately a false oath on a religion other than Islam would become that which he had professed. And he who killed himself with anything Allah would torment him with that in the Fire of Hell"""
"1617","[AI-translation] Bara, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, peace be upon him, said to Hassan: ""Satirize them, or attack them, and Jibril is with you.""
1618"""
"1618","Narrated 'Urwah: I set about abusing Hassan in the presence of 'Aishah, and she said, ""Do not abuse him, for he used to defend the Prophet (ﷺ)."""
"1619","[AI-translation] Narrated Aishah from Masruq who said: We entered upon Aishah, and with her was Hassan ibn Thabit, reciting poetry to her, improvising verses of his. He said: ""A chaste, dignified woman, untainted by suspicion, who wakes hungry from [abstaining from] the flesh of the ignorant."" Aishah said to him: ""But you are not like that."" Masruq said: So I said to her: ""Why do you permit him to enter upon you when Allah, the Exalted, has said, 'And he who took upon himself the greatest part of it among them will have a grievous punishment'?"" She said: ""And what punishment is harsher than blindness?"" She said to him: ""He used to defend, or argue on behalf of, the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him.""
1620"""
"1620","Narrated 'Aisha: Hassan asked the permission of the Prophet (ﷺ) to satirize the disbelievers. The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""What about my lineage?"" Hassan said, ""I will extract you from them just as a hair is extracted from dough."""
"1621","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurayrah: You claim that Abu Hurayrah narrates abundantly from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him; by Allah, the appointment is set. I was a poor man, keeping company with the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, on a full stomach, while the Muhajirun were occupied with trading in the markets, and the Ansar were occupied with tending to their wealth. I was present with the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, one day when he said: ""Whoever spreads his cloak until I finish my speech, then folds it over himself, will not forget anything he has heard from me."" So I spread a cloak that was on me, and by the One who sent him with the truth, I did not forget anything I heard from him.""
1622"""
"1622","Narrated 'Ali (رضي الله عنه): The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent me, Az-Zubair, and Al-Miqdad bin Al-Aswad, saying, ""Proceed till you reach Rawdat Khakh, for there is a woman there carrying a letter, so take it from her."" So we set off, our horses galloping, until we reached the Rawdah, and there we found the woman. We said, ""Bring out the letter."" She said, ""I have no letter with me."" We said, ""Either you bring out the letter, or we will take off your clothes."" So she took it out from her braided hair. We brought the letter to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and in it was written: From Hatib bin Abi Balta'ah to some of the pagans of Makkah, informing them of some of the affairs of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""O Hatib! What is this?"" He said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Do not be hasty in judging me. I was a man attached to Quraish but was not one of them (i.e., I was an adherent but not a blood relative), while the emigrants who are with you have relatives in Makkah who protect their families and properties. So, since I lacked blood relations with them, I wanted to do them a favor so that they might protect my relatives. I did not do this because of disbelief or apostasy, nor because of preferring disbelief after Islam."" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""He has told you the truth."" 'Umar said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Let me strike off the neck of this hypocrite!"" The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""He was present at Badr, and how do you know? Perhaps Allah looked upon the people of Badr and said, 'Do what you wish, for I have forgiven you.'"""
"1623","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him: I was with the Prophet, peace be upon him, while he was encamped at al-Ji'ranah, between Makkah and Madinah, and Bilal was with him. A bedouin came to the Prophet, peace be upon him, and said: ""Will you not fulfill for me what you promised me?"" He said to him: ""Glad tidings!"" The bedouin said: ""You have said 'glad tidings' to me too many times."" He turned to Abu Musa and Bilal, appearing angry, and said: ""He has rejected the glad tidings, so accept them, you two."" They said: ""We accept."" Then he called for a vessel of water, washed his hands and face in it, and spat into it. Then he said: ""Drink from it, and pour it over your faces and chests, and receive glad tidings."" They took the vessel and did so. Umm Salamah called out from behind the screen: ""Leave some for your mother!"" So they left a portion of it for her.""
1624"""
"1624","Narrated Abu Musa (May Allah be pleased with him): When the Prophet (ﷺ) finished with (the battle of) Hunain, he sent Abu 'Amir at the head of an army to Autas. He met Duraid bin As-Simma, and Duraid was killed and Allah routed his companions.

Abu Musa said: He sent me along with Abu 'Amir. Abu 'Amir was struck in the knee by an arrow, a man from the tribe of Jusham shot him and fixed the arrow in his knee. I went to him and said, ""O uncle, who shot you?"" He pointed to me (indicating the man) and said, ""That is the one who killed me."" So I made for him and pursued him, and when he saw me, he fled. I followed him and kept saying to him, ""Are you not ashamed? Will you not stand firm?"" So he stopped, and we exchanged two blows with our swords, and I killed him. Then I said to Abu 'Amir, ""Allah has killed your enemy.""

He said, ""Then pull out this arrow."" So I pulled it out, and water gushed forth from it. He said, ""O son of my brother, convey my greeting of peace to the Prophet (ﷺ) and tell him: 'Ask forgiveness for me.'"" Abu 'Amir appointed me to be in charge of the people (in his place). He remained (alive) for a short while, then he died.

I returned and went in to see the Prophet (ﷺ) in his house, (where he was lying) on a bed of plaited palm leaves, with only a mat spread over it, so that the marks of the plaited leaves had left imprints on his back and sides. I informed him of our news and of the news of Abu 'Amir, and said, ""He told me to say to you: Ask forgiveness for me.""

The Prophet (ﷺ) called for water, performed ablution with it, then raised his hands and said, ""O Allah, forgive Ubaid, Abu 'Amir, his sins."" I saw the whiteness of his armpits (as he raised his hands). Then he said, ""O Allah, on the Day of Resurrection, make him rank above many of Your creatures among mankind.""

I said, ""And (ask forgiveness) for me too."" So he said, ""O Allah, forgive the sin of 'Abdullah bin Qais, and admit him on the Day of Resurrection to a honourable entrance.""

Abu Burda (the narrator of the Hadith) said: One of these two supplications was for Abu 'Amir, and the other was for Abu Musa."
"1625","Hadith of Abu Musa: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""I recognize the voices of the group of Al-Ash'ariyyin by their recitation of the Quran when they enter at night, and I recognize their dwellings from their voices reciting the Quran at night, even though I had not seen their dwellings when they alighted during the day. And among them is Hakeem, who when he meets the cavalry (or he said) the enemy, says to them: 'My companions order you to wait for them.'"""""""
"1626","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, When the people of Ash`ari tribe ran short of food during the holy battles"""
"1627","Anas reported that the people of Yemen came to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) and said:Send with us a person who should teach us Sunnah and al-Islam, whereupon he (the Holy Prophet) caught hold of the hand of Ubaida and said: He is a man of trust of this Umma"""
"1628","This Verse: ""When two of your parties almost Decided to fall away..."" was revealed in our connection, i.e. Bani Salama and Bani Haritha and I would not have liked that, if it was not revealed, for Allah said:-- But Allah was their Protector.....(3.122)"""
"1629","`Abdullah bin Al-Fadl told me that Anas bin Malik said, I was much grieve over those who had been killed in the Battle of Al-Harra. When Zaid bin Arqarr heard of my intense grief (over the killed Ansar)"""
"1630","Al-Bara' b. Azib reported:I saw Hasan b. 'Ali upon the shoulders of Allah's Apostle (ﷺ) and he was saying: O Allah, I love him, and love him Thou"""
"1631","Once an Ansari woman, accompanied by a son of hers, came to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ). Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) spoke to her and said twice, By Him in Whose Hand my life is"""
"1632","Abu Said al-Khudri reported:'Ali b. Abu Talib sent to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) from Yemen some gold alloyed with clay in a leather bag dyed in the leaves of Mimosa flava. He distributed it among four men. 'Uyaina b. Hisna, Aqra' b. Habis and Zaid al-Khail, and the fourth one was either Alqama b. 'Ulatha or 'Amir b. Tufail. A person from among his (Prophet's) Companions said: We had a better claim to this (wealth) than these (persons). This (remark) reached the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) upon which he said: Will you not trust me, whereas I am a trustee of Him Who is in the heaven? The news come to me from the heaven morning and evening. Then there stood up a person with deep sunken eyes, prominent cheek bones, and elevated forehead, thick beard, shaven head, tucked up loincloth, and he said: Messenger of Allah, fear Allah. He (the Holy Prophet) said: Woe to thee. Do I not deserve most to fear Allah amongst the people of the earth? That man then returned. Khalid b. Walid then said: Messenger of Allah, should I not strike his neck? Upon this he (the Holy Prophet) said: Perhaps he may be observing the prayer. Khalid said: How many observers of prayer are there who profess with their tongue what is not in their heart? Upon this the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: I have not been commanded to pierce through the hearts of people, nor to split their bellies (insides). He again looked at him and he was going back. Upon this he (the Holy Prophet) said: There would arise a people from the progeny of this (man) who would recite the Qur'an glibly, but it would not go beyond their throats; they would (hurriedly) pass through (the teachings of their) religion just as the arrow passes through the prey. I conceive that he (the Holy Prophet) also said this: If I find them I would certainly kill them as were killed the (people of) Thamud"""
"1633","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, The best family among the Ansar is the Banu An-Najjar. """""" ""1634"",A hadith like this has been transmitted by Abual-Rahman al-Araj on the authority of Abu Huraira"""
"1634","[AI-translation] Narrated Jarir ibn Abdullah from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I accompanied Jarir ibn Abdullah, and he used to serve me, and he was older than Anas. Jarir said: ""I saw the Ansar doing something, such that I do not find anyone among them except that I honor him.""
1635"""
"1635","Narrated Abu Hurairah (رضي الله عنه): The Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Aslam, may Allah keep them safe; and Ghifar, may Allah forgive them."""
"1636","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn Umar: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said on the pulpit: ""Ghifar, may Allah forgive them; Aslam, may Allah grant them peace; and 'Usayyah, they have disobeyed Allah and His Messenger.""
1637"""
"1637","Narrated Abu Hurairah: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""Quraish, the Ansar, Juhainah, Muzainah, Aslam, Ashja' and Ghifar are my allies (Mawali), and they have no ally besides Allah and His Messenger."""
"1638","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Aslam, Ghifar, and a portion of Muzaynah and Juhaynah—or he said: a portion of Juhaynah or Muzaynah—are better before Allah—or he said: on the Day of Resurrection—than Asad, Tamim, Hawazin, and Ghatafan.""
1639"""
"1639","Narrated Abu Bakrah: Al-Aqra' bin Habis said to the Prophet (ﷺ): ""None have given you the pledge of allegiance except the thieves who rob the pilgrims, from Aslam, Ghifar, Muzainah and Juhainah."" The Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""What do you think if Aslam, Ghifar, Muzainah and Juhainah were better than Banu Tamim, Banu 'Amir, Asad and Ghatafan - would they have failed and lost?"" He said: ""Yes."" The Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""By Him in Whose Hand my soul is, they are indeed better than them."""
"1640","Narrated Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him): Tufail bin 'Amr Ad-Dausi and his companions came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said, ""O Allah's Messenger! Daus (the tribe) has disobeyed and refused (to accept Islam), so invoke Allah's wrath upon them."" It was said, ""Daus is destroyed!"" He said, ""O Allah, guide Daus and bring them (to Islam)."""
"1641","I have loved the people of the tribe of Bani Tamim ever since I heard, three things, Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said about them. I heard him saying, These people (of the tribe of Bani Tamim) would stand firm against Ad-Dajjal. When the Sadaqat (gifts of charity) from that tribe came"""
"1642","A'isha reported:I heard that never a prophet dies until he is given an option to opt the life of (this) world or that of the Hereafter. She further said: I heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) say in his last illness in which he' died. I heard him saying in gruffness of the voice: Along with those persons upon whom Allah bestowed favours from amongst the Apostles, the testifiers of truth, the martyrs, the pious and goodly company are they (iv. 69). (It was on bearing these words) that I thought that he had been given choice (and he opted to live with these pious persons in the Paradise)"""
"1643","I heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) saying, The good deeds of any person will not make him enter Paradise."" (i.e."""
"1644","Narrated `Asim:\n\nI heard Anas bin Malik, \Have you ever heard that the Prophet (ﷺ) said"""
"1645","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) was asked, Who is the most honorable amongst the people?"" He replied"""
"1646","The hadith of ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him, who said: ""The best of people is my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then there will come a people whose testimony will precede his oath, and his oath will be testimony."""""""
"1647","I heard `Imran bin Husain saying, ""The Prophet (ﷺ) said, 'The best people are those living in my generation, then those coming after them, and then those coming after (the second generation)."" `Imran said ""I do not know whether the Prophet (ﷺ) mentioned two or three generations after your present generation. The Prophet (ﷺ) added, 'There will be some people after you, who will be dishonest and will not be trustworthy and will give witness (evidences) without being asked to give witness, and will vow but will not fulfill their vows, and obesity will appear among them."""" ""1648"",Jabir b. 'Abdullah reported:Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) led us in the 'Id prayer in Medina on the Day of Sacrifice. Some persons slaughtered their animals ahead of him under the impression that Allah's Apostle (ﷺ) had-already offered sacrifice. Thereupon Allah's Apostle (ﷺ) said: Those who had slaughtered their animals ahead of him should slaughter the other ones in their stead. And they should not sacrifice the animal before Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) had sacrificed (his animal)"""
"1648","[AI-translation] Hadith of 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, led us in the 'Isha' prayer at the end of his life. When he uttered the salam, he stood up and said: ""Do you see this night of yours? For at the turn of a hundred years from it, no one will remain on the surface of the earth.""
1649"""
"1649","Narrated Abu Sa'id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""Do not abuse my companions! If anyone of you spent gold equal to Mount Uhud in charity, it would not equal a Mudd (a small measure of grain) spent by one of them, nor even half of it."""
"1650","Narrated Abu Huraira:\n\nWhile we were sitting with the Prophet (ﷺ) Surat Al-Jumu'a was revealed to him, and when the Verse, \n\And He (Allah) has sent him (Muhammad) also to other (Muslims).....' (62.3) was recited by the \nProphet"""
"1651","That while he was included in a delegation of Quraish staying with Muawiya, Muawiya heard that `Abdullah bin `Amr had said that there would be a king from Qahtan tribe, whereupon he became very angry. He stood up, and after glorifying and praising Allah as He deserved, said, To proceed"""
"1652","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said on the Day of (the battle of) Hunain, Whoever has killed an infidel and has a proof or a witness for it"""
